344. -I. Power to make rules. -
(1)
The Central Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, make rules to carry out the purposes of this Part.
(2)
In particular and without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing power, such rules may provide for all or any of the
following matters, namely:-
(a)
the design, construction and standards of inspection and assembly of the reactor installations of nuclear ships;
